        body: 'When Micah finished his paragraph he read it to his little sister, who was nine and had been told she could ask one question after every sentence, and the question was always the same: how do you know? For the first sentence he said: a letter written the next winter by a man who was there. For the second: the same letter. For the third he opened his mouth and nothing came out, because the third sentence had come from a poster. He crossed it out. The fourth had a court paper behind it. The fifth had two. When he was done there were four sentences and four answers, and his sister said it was shorter than before, and he said that was the point.',
